<!--
  Joint <limit> values are referenced to the joint zero (q = 0 = CAD assembly pose, the
  retracted end of the mechanical stroke).  They are derived from the two stroke-end
  ABSOLUTE link angles recorded in 底盘数据.txt: for a hip, the travel is the change of the
  ham angle; for a knee it is the change of the calf angle RELATIVE to the ham
  (dq = d(calf) - d(ham), ~114.5 deg), because the ham itself rotates too.  The knee values
  are taken from the closed-loop-consistent pose at the stroke end.  The full mechanical
  stroke is preserved (leg length 144.8 mm -> 389.7 mm) and q = 0 lies inside every range;
  read literally as absolute angles, the old values put q = 0 outside six joints and PhysX
  clamped the mechanism on the first step.
-->
